Nina (Docs): Opened tiny follow-up PR to err-ref: compact examples for 429 handling + stream resume. PR #8281.
Dev (Eng Docs): Can we keep examples micro: one sync retry snippet parsing Retry-After/x-rw-retry, one streaming resume using resume_token + kv hint?
Ava (SDK): I'll add TS + Python inline snippets. Note: show Retry-After precedence then x-rw-retry. Mention SDK helper retryWithBackoff.
Leo (Runtime): Runtime now emits resume_token in stream footer on truncation — recommend using it to resume. Add a note about passing kv_cache hints to improve cache hits.
Ava (SDK): Draft TS snippet (TS SDK >=3.2):
```ts
// parse headers, retry up to 3 times
async function sendWithRetry(req){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    const res = await client.generate(req)
    if(res.status===429){
      const delay = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after']||res.headers['x-rw-retry']||'1')
      await sleep(delay*1000*Math.pow(2,i))
      continue
    }
    return res
  }
  throw new Error('rate limited')
}
```
